IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fbtaa-employee`
IMPORT `fbtaa-seat-employer`

-- Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 -- worked cases, from the seat of the employer. Every assertion is a claim about
-- the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand from the deposited text and the
-- formulas sidecar, never copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL. GST is taken at 10%.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The taxable amount, s 5B. FBT year 2026, FBT rate 47%, GST rate 10%.
-- The type 1 factor is (0.47 + 0.1) / ((1 - 0.47) x (1 + 0.1) x 0.47) = 0.57 / 0.27401, so a type 1 amount of $27,401
-- grosses up to $57,000. The type 2 factor is 1 / 0.53, so a type 2 amount of $5,300 grosses up to $10,000. Together $67,000.
#ASSERT `As the employer, my fringe benefits taxable amount` 2026 27401 5300 0.1 EQUALS `answered` 67000
#ASSERT `As the employer, my fringe benefits taxable amount` 2026 0 5300 0.1 EQUALS `answered` 10000
-- The tax: 47% of $67,000 = $31,490.
#ASSERT `As the employer, the fringe benefits tax I must pay` 2026 27401 5300 0.1 EQUALS `answered` 31490
-- FBT year 2016, rate 49%: type 2 of $5,100 grosses up to $10,000 (1/0.51); tax $4,900.
#ASSERT `As the employer, my fringe benefits taxable amount` 2016 0 5100 0.1 EQUALS `answered` 10000
#ASSERT `As the employer, the fringe benefits tax I must pay` 2016 0 5100 0.1 EQUALS `answered` 4900
#ASSERT `As the employer, the fringe benefits tax I must pay` 2013 0 5100 0.1 EQUALS `not covered` `the deposited Fringe Benefits Tax Act gives the rate only for years of tax from 1 April 2015`

-- Return and payment for the FBT year starting 1 April 2026: 21 May 2027 (ss 68, 90).
#ASSERT `As the employer, the day my FBT return and tax are due` 2026 EQUALS Date 21 5 2027

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- MIRROR CASES: the same facts asked from both seats, with answers that agree.
-- The $60,000 car first held on 1 May 2020, $1,500 tow bar, all year 2026: $8,300 from both seats.
#ASSERT `As the employer, the taxable value of the car` 60000 (Date 1 5 2020) 2026 1500 365 0 EQUALS 8300
#ASSERT `The taxable value of my car` 60000 (Date 1 5 2020) 2026 1500 365 0 EQUALS 8300
-- The $50,000 car, 183 of 366 days in 2027: $5,000 from both seats.
#ASSERT `As the employer, the taxable value of the car` 50000 (Date 15 6 2026) 2027 0 183 0 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `The taxable value of my car` 50000 (Date 15 6 2026) 2027 0 183 0 EQUALS 5000
-- The $100,000 interest-free loan at a hypothetical 9%, all year: $9,000 from both seats.
#ASSERT `As the employer, the taxable value of the loan` 100000 365 9 0 EQUALS 9000
#ASSERT `The taxable value of my loan` 100000 365 9 0 EQUALS 9000
-- A battery electric car, no luxury car tax: exempt, from both seats; a plug-in hybrid: not.
#ASSERT `As the employer, is the electric car exempt` TRUE `a battery electric vehicle (electric motor only, no fuel cell or petrol or diesel engine)` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the car benefit is exempt (s 8A), but its taxable value still counts towards my reportable fringe benefits amount (s 135P(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my electric car exempt` TRUE `a battery electric vehicle (electric motor only, no fuel cell or petrol or diesel engine)` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the car benefit is exempt (s 8A), but its taxable value still counts towards my reportable fringe benefits amount (s 135P(3))`
#ASSERT `As the employer, is the electric car exempt` TRUE `a plug-in hybrid` FALSE EQUALS `no: only a battery electric or hydrogen fuel cell electric vehicle is a zero or low emissions vehicle (s 8A(2)-(4)); a plug-in hybrid or other car is not`
-- The reportable amount on $5,300 in 2026: $10,000 from both seats; on $2,000: none; on $8,480 (for example an exempt
-- electric car, which still counts under s 135P(3)): $16,000.
#ASSERT `As the employer, the reportable fringe benefits amount` 5300 2026 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 10000
#ASSERT `My reportable fringe benefits amount` 5300 2026 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 10000
#ASSERT `As the employer, the reportable fringe benefits amount` 2000 2026 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `As the employer, the reportable fringe benefits amount` 8480 2026 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 16000
